# Freeze the DEX-13 orc warrior tools/keys/dequ-save-dc-setup.keys builds, so
# tools/check_dequ_save_dc.sh loads him instead of rolling him again (bd inc-cr8v).
#
#   tools/make_char_fixture.sh dequ-save-dc-seed5-opt0822 \
#       tools/keys/dequ-save-dc-save.keys 5 tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat
#
# THE CHARGEN BELOW IS A COPY of tools/keys/dequ-save-dc-setup.keys up to the
# point where it opens wizard mode, unchanged. The attribute row
# "16 13 15 14 13 10 14" (STR 16, DEX 13) exists only on seed 5, which is why the
# fixture is made on seed 5 and why the check no longer rolls him: on any other
# seed the row is absent and @cursorto:mark finds nothing. Part A of the check
# wants a mid-DEX Reflex save (a +1 modifier, a predicted 45-60% pass rate).

@expect "Initial Choices"
a       # Initial Choices: start menu is not a screen @choose reads.
@expect "Alter the character generation options?"
n       # No: this is a yes/no question.
@expect "Explore Mode. Continue?"
y       # Yes: this is a yes/no question.
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Warrior"
@expect "Which of the five attribute sets"
# Select the set whose DEX is 13, a mid-Dex melee build, by the values it
# shows and not by its position. The five sets are rolled, so any change to
# the RNG stream (appending a resource to lib/, for one) moves them: on seed 5
# the DEX-13 set was fifth and is now fourth (inc-s1qj). The row reads
# "16 13 15 14 13 10 14" (STR DEX CON INT WIS CHA LUC); walk the marker onto
# it and confirm. Selecting by letter here would be selecting by position.
@cursorto:mark "16  13  15  14  13  10  14" DOWN
ENTER
@choose "Chaotic Good"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
@expect "Skill Manager"
ENTER   # Finish allocating ranks: a control key, not a named choice.
@expect "Confirm keep changes to skill ranks?"
y       # Keep the ranks: this is a yes/no question.
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
@expect "Your personality archetype"
# Personality affects only the sheet banner, so its selection is not pinned.
ENTER   # Accept the selected personality archetype.
@expect "Entry Chamber"
y       # Dismiss the Entry Chamber description.
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
@expect "Things in View"
ENTER   # Try to enter something here; the game refuses.
@expect "You can't go in anything here."
y       # Open the dungeon verb menu.
@expect "What do you want to do?"
a       # In-game [a] Apply: keep this key before ESC closes the menu.
# Three plain ESCs close the Apply menu and any follow-up prompt whatever the
# starting kit, because a narrow menu leaves "Things in View" visible.
ESC
ESC
ESC


@until "System Menu" ESC
@expect "System Menu"
b       # [b] Save and Continue; no @quit, so the run ends with one save.
